meta {
  name: Add Household Member
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/households/{{householdId}}/members
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "firstName": "Dana",
    "lastName": "Tyson",
    "dateOfBirth": "1974-03-09",
    "role": "Spouse"
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 201 Created", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201);
  });

  test("returns the new member as a ContactSummary", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body).to.have.property("id");
    expect(body.firstName).to.equal("Dana");
    expect(body.lastName).to.equal("Tyson");
    expect(body.roleInHousehold).to.equal("Spouse");
    expect(body.emails).to.be.an("array");
    expect(body.phones).to.be.an("array");
  });

  test("a member is never the primary contact", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().isPrimary).to.equal(false);
  });

  test("the date of birth is stored as the calendar day sent, not shifted", function () {
    // Parsed to UTC midnight from explicit components. `new Date("1974-03-09")`
    // through a timezone west of Greenwich would land on the 8th.
    expect(res.getBody().dateOfBirth).to.contain("1974-03-09");
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /households/:id/members

  Add a member to a household — the **"+ Member"** dialog on the Household
  Details page (`/clients/:id`). A member *is* a `Contact`; there is no separate
  member record.

  - **Module:** `clients` (the class-level OR-gate also accepts `crm_service`
    for the **reads** on this controller, but this write does not).
  - **Permission:** `clients:write`. `crm_service:read` alone cannot reach it.
  - **Data scope:** the household is loaded through the same scope filter as
    `GET /households/:id` — `own` collapses to branch on client records. Out of
    scope reads as 404.

  ## Body
  | Field | Required | Notes |
  |---|---|---|
  | `firstName` | yes | 1–60 chars, trimmed |
  | `lastName` | yes | 1–60 chars, trimmed |
  | `dateOfBirth` | no | `YYYY-MM-DD`. Members often have none on file |
  | `role` | yes | One of `HOUSEHOLD_MEMBER_ROLES`: `Spouse`, `Child`, `Driver`, `Additional Named Insured` |

  `Named Insured` is **rejected**. It is the primary contact's role, implied by
  `contacts.isPrimary` and stamped by lead intake; accepting it here would give
  a household two primaries.

  ## What it writes
  Two documents, both required — the contact's `householdId` is what the
  household page reads, while `memberContactIds` is what the lead-intake
  pipeline and the migration maintain:

  1. A `Contact` with `isPrimary: false`, `roleInHousehold: <role>`, and the
     household's own `agencyId` / `branchId` (never the caller's).
  2. `$addToSet` of the new contact id onto the household's `memberContactIds`.

  Deliberately **not** deduplicated against existing contacts, unlike the public
  intake pipeline: this is a human on the household's own page who can already
  see its members listed, so silently merging into a same-named contact would be
  the surprising outcome.

  ## Response
  `ContactSummary` — the same shape `GET /households/:id` lists members in.

  ## Errors
  | Status | When |
  |---|---|
  | 400 | Missing/blank name, `role` outside the enum, malformed `dateOfBirth` |
  | 401 | Missing/expired bearer token |
  | 403 | `clients` disabled for the agency, or the caller lacks `clients:write` |
  | 404 | Unknown household, malformed id, or a household outside the caller's scope |
}
